WEBVTT

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.220
By the way, Hasegawa hasn't said a word

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.700
about that night since it happened.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.570
She probably blanked her mind

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.120
of all memories from that night.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:21.780
Just like her.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.000
The smart ones get over things quick.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.170
Oh yeah, Sawaki...

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.270
Could you substitute for 
me in our afternoon class?

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.550
Huh? Me?

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.150
For me, too!

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:34.010
Fine...

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.690
Moyashimon

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:58.970
Cling to That Soft Skin

00:01:56.530 --> 00:02:00.550
All right, we did it! 
We passed the interview!

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:03.430
Sawaki, were you able to cover for us?

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:05.990
No, it didn't work at all.

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:06.930
Idiot!

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:09.560
You made your underclassman do that?

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.320
Hey, don't say that. 
Today is a day to celebrate.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.150
If you're celebrating something,

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.940
why don't we open these?

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.330
Surstromming?

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.250
Isn't it "Surströmming"?

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.330
That's how they pronounced 
it in its native country.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:30.620
Sounds like I don't need 
to explain it to you all.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:33.340
This is a Swedish canned product 
known as the smelliest food in the world.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.200
The cans have fully expanded.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.030
It's the perfect time to eat it.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.060
I suspected this day would come,

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.470
but this is sort of sudden...

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.070
Because of its powerful 
characteristics,

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:46.600
many TV shows often treat 
this product as a plaything.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:51.320
Its true nature is too 
frequently ignored.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.110
We are researchers of fermentation.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.640
I believe we should face this

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.490
marvelous product 
seriously, not as a game.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:00.860
I agree.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:04.240
Serious or not, 
if it stinks, it stinks.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.850
Peel the potatoes after they're boiled.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:09.870
Okay.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.270
Pull it off.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:14.710
Ow! Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.800
Can't! Can't! Hot! Hot!

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.090
And, Kawahama, you take these.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.070
So what are we celebrating?

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:23.590
We passed an interview 
for a part-time job.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:24.950
A job?

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.250
Yeah.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.810
We've got underclassmen now,

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.880
so we need to build up war funds.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.590
Don't tell the first-years about this.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:35.350
I wouldn't tell them 
something that pointless.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:39.010
You can't help your underclassmen 
much with their studies,

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:41.360
so you should make up for 
it with financial support.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.550
We will.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:45.760
So you should be the one to 
help them with their studies.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.930
Even if we treat them 
every now and then,

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.080
you're probably the one they respect.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.580
So let's use teamwork, okay?

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.240
Despite how they look,

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:02.510
I guess they really do 
understand their position.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.590
Now I sound like I was just being sarcastic.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.850
Well, the side dishes are all ready.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.040
Time to open one...

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.940
Mutou-kun.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.850
Hold on a minute, Professor...

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:16.390
Don't worry.

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:18.610
I'll give you a poncho and vinyl gloves.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.290
Go ahead.

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:21.360
Right...

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.420
On TV, they often show 
the liquid contents

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:30.350
squirting out of the 
can when it's opened,

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:32.620
but that's all just an act for TV.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.700
If you tilt the can 45 degrees

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:38.360
Contents

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:38.380
and just poke a tiny hole 
in it, it won't splatter.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.550
Y-You liar.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.680
Ugh, it stinks!

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.070
Are you okay?

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.800
This one's nearing its limit, 
so you can have it.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.430
O-Okay...

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.710
By the way, this fall, 
we're going to start making

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:17.210
a real batch of 
university-produced sake.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.590
So it's finally going to get started.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.930
You'd better make yourself useful.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.210
Uh, right.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.250
But we won't need Sawaki-kun's ability

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.770
to make sake in our fermenting cellar.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.640
His ability?

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.220
His ability to see microbes, of course.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:36.870
If we use that, everything 
will go too smoothly.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:40.360
It'll be more fun if everyone 
works hard together.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.360
Oh... I guess that's true.

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.850
But without your ability 
to see microbes,

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:48.680
what good are you?

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.240
<i>I went overboard again...</i>

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.750
Oh, Hasegawa-kun, 
isn't it about that time?

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:01.480
Yes, though, as usual, 
I'm not really up for it.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.630
I'll just think of it as 
another typical lecture.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:10.140
57th Floor.

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:18.300
Welcome, Miss Haruka.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.650
The other two are waiting at the table.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:22.400
Stiffs.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.690
Miss Haruka.

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:27.270
Welcome.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:30.570
Please enjoy the meal to 
your heart's content.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.950
Fire these two this instant!

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.660
What the hell for, stupid Haruka?!

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:38.540
What are you two little 
cockroaches doing here?!

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:42.420
Teamwork! Teamwork, 
Researcher Hasegawa!

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:44.290
What are you doing?!

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:46.550
Why are we actually getting fired?!

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:50.050
How powerful is the 
Hasegawa family, anyway?!

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:53.150
The quality of this 
restaurant has declined.

00:06:53.150 --> 00:06:54.930
Make those two leave immediately.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.310
Of course. I sincerely apologize.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.020
Cut the crap!

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:02.310
We won't be satisfied until 
we get to eat something!

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.770
That's right! We're not 
employees anymore,

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.280
we're customers! Give us a menu!

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.060
What are you talking about?!

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:08.320
The whole restaurant 
is reserved for them!

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:12.530
I don't mind. I'm the one 
who blurted that out.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:15.390
Besides, it's not like this is 
a party or a family dinner.

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:17.080
It was silly to reserve 
the whole place.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.340
Haruka!

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:20.830
Oh, it's all right, Father.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.700
Give those two a menu.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:26.090
At least it won't be so stiff in here.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.730
Certainly.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:29.320
You there!

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:30.090
Yes, sir.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.340
An appetizer alone is 8,000 yen?

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:35.170
Insane. This restaurant is insane.

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:37.180
Two drafts and some mixed nuts.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.850
One beer is enough!

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:43.470
Give them the same meal I'm getting.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:45.040
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:49.480
Are they students at your university?

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:52.990
Yes. They're in Professor Itsuki's 
pre-seminar, and they're idiots.

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:55.420
It's been long enough, Haruka.

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:57.240
Quit that school by this summer.

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:00.420
I'd rather you uphold 
your original promise.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.870
You said I could do as I please 
until I graduate, right?

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:06.980
Who said you could start 
a doctoral program?

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:09.000
You said until I graduate.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.310
What I do until then is my choice.

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:13.390
I have no intention of 
playing word games!

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:15.650
Why did you abandon the school 
you attended from kindergarten

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:18.140
to high school and choose 
an agricultural university?

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:22.920
What's more, I hear you've been 
wearing immodest attire in public.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:24.520
Thanks, researcher!

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.230
It's deplorable!

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:29.030
Have you never considered 
Ryuuta-kun's feelings?

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:31.650
Please, Father...

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.340
May I speak, as well?

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.310
Thanks to your father's assistance,

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:38.530
my own business is increasingly stable.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:43.880
I feel prepared to welcome the 
woman I love into my life.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:48.880
All that's left is to wait 
until you finish school.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.800
I won't tell you to quit right away.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:55.300
Sometimes it's necessary 
to take detours in life.

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:57.050
Detours?

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.710
Isn't that what it is?

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:01.110
College is a place for young people

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:02.980
who haven't decided on their own futures

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:05.710
to find where they wish to go in life.

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:07.750
College isn't a detour!

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.690
That's right! It's life itself!

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:13.820
Your father and I have arranged

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:16.450
a wonderful life for you, Haruka-san.

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:21.190
So long as that Professor 
Itsuki doesn't tempt her.

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:23.800
Although I acknowledge his history

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:26.080
and his expansive connections...

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.580
Oh, no.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.820
Associating with an 
eccentric man like him

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:31.920
will broaden Haruka-san's experience.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:35.200
Of course, I do wish she'd 
do so in moderation...

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:35.970
Yes.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.210
I won't allow you to 
insult Professor Itsuki.

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:43.220
He has been a far better role model 
for me than the two of you.

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:46.590
Haruka!

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:48.730
I'm going to the powder 
room. I'll be right back.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.110
Hey. Come with me.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.280
You, too!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.230
Wha...

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.610
You're not supposed to actually pee!

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:05.200
Anyway, your family's really something.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.110
We listened in.

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:09.960
So people still arrange marriages 
in this day and age...

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.750
It's just nepotism.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:14.840
More importantly, you should 
get me out of here.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.090
What?

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:19.310
I've heard what they wanted to say.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:22.260
But it would still be rude to walk out

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.150
when my father reserved my seat.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:26.470
What?

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.980
I can't come up with anything if you 
ask me out of nowhere like that...

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:32.200
Our best plan so far is to

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:34.270
have you burst in and 
invite her to dance,

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:36.120
and have her dance right 
out of the restaurant.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:39.240
I don't know if that's a plan 
worthy of a celebrity, though...

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.690
I don't know if it is either,

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:45.240
but wouldn't something more 
like an accident be better?

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.630
Come up with something for us!

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:50.000
What? I have to think of something?

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:52.110
It's really tight.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:53.130
What's wrong?

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.400
Oh... nothing.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:58.130
Well, something just occurred to me...

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:01.640
57th Floor.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:11.620
I'm very sorry. This restaurant 
is reserved for the night.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:15.550
There should be two guys in there 
named Misato and Kawahama.

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:17.390
They asked me to bring this for them.

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:18.690
I understand, sir.

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:20.680
I'll take care of it.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:23.250
Please wait here for a moment.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.020
I'm so sorry.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:33.410
Hurry up...

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:36.210
Now!

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.210
Over here!

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:47.040
Doing something like that 
to any food is blasphemy.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:49.330
Good job, though, Sawaki.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:53.500
They were pouring alcohol 
on the can in a heartbeat.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:54.870
Talk about true chefs.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:57.890
I'd have been better 
off just walking out.

00:11:57.890 --> 00:11:59.780
We were already on dessert.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:02.150
Why are you so uncute?

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:05.930
I know, I know! 
I owe it all to you guys!

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.160
I'll buy you dinner or 
whatever it is you want!

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:12.720
Just... no alcohol.

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:15.000
I'll tell you guys since you've seen it,

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.790
but I get sort of needy.

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:18.800
Needy?

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.390
Misato!

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:22.080
I only heard that you got your ear

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:24.550
and nose bitten off, but then...

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:26.340
Don't kid around!

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:27.930
How do you call that "needy"?!

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:30.310
What's your problem?! 
What would you call it, then?

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:31.110
Extreme sadism!

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:32.810
And what's that supposed to mean?!

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:36.730
Nothing To Do But Attack

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.990
Oh? I see you've got a couple 
of rare customers tonight.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:46.110
Looks like whoever they're 
waiting for didn't show.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:48.760
I told you,

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:51.270
don't spout nonsense just 
because I don't remember!

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:52.560
It's not nonsense!

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:55.410
That was not being needy! 
You're a sadist!

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:56.680
All right, who cares?

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.750
You still have to come to the party!

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.680
Shut up! I know that!

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:03.260
I don't want this debt to linger.

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:06.680
Welcome.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.760
Ah, Princess, this is a rare visit.

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:11.260
It's not rare! It's a first!

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:13.170
Don't make a fuss.

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:16.270
Those two boys have 
been waiting for you.

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:22.900
Looks like that party 
was a dismal failure.

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:25.110
Sawaki.

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:27.560
Come join me.

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:28.280
Huh?

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:30.740
Those two have barely said a word.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.920
Do something to liven things up.

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:36.960
Just come on.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:38.670
But I don't think I can...

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:42.040
That's unusual. 
Hasegawa-kun looks troubled.

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:43.670
Yeah. Isn't it cute?

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:49.050
I guess those two aren't 
very good at communicating.

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:53.590
Hasegawa-kun has always 
done everything alone,

00:13:53.590 --> 00:13:55.930
and Sawaki-kun has always relied

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:57.440
on his childhood friend, Yuuki-kun.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.310
That's not such a big problem.

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:03.120
You're right.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:04.880
Those two birds are destined to

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:06.950
leave their cages and fly much higher.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.880
I just hope that,

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:11.490
once they've flown to 
their hearts' content,

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:14.570
they'll return to my shoulder 
when they get hungry.

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:21.500
What a day.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:25.260
I'll never get to sleep at this rate.

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:29.760
Today was sort of tiring.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.770
Miso

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:40.270
Kei's not answering...

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:46.030
So, Hasegawa-san, how long have 
you known Professor Itsuki?

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:51.030
Since I was 14, so about 10 years now.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:52.760
Wow, that long?

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:55.100
And do you and Mutou-san both

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:58.040
plan to stay in his lab from now on?

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:00.920
I guess so...

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:05.500
I was thinking of checking out 
the employment office soon.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:08.700
What? Weren't you going to 
continue with graduate school?

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.550
I haven't made any decisions yet.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.430
That makes sense.

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:20.290
Sorry, but I'm going to bed.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:21.290
Huh?

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.070
Mind if I drink a little more?

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:29.690
Huh? Oh... sure.

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:36.330
Hey... don't you think 
Hasegawa-san is acting strangely?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:39.020
Wow, there's still five bottles left!

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:45.830
I guess I'm just a bird in a cage...

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:56.260
Hasegawa Haruka-chan, correct?

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:59.510
I don't know what's wrong,

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:01.250
but this is your father's party.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:02.450
Aren't you going to eat?

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.520
I don't want to. Nothing tastes good.

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:08.120
Well, I suppose if the 
hotel's food tastes bad,

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:10.530
there won't be anything you like.

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:12.850
Who are you?

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:14.530
Do you work with my father?

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:18.850
I'm like a friend of a friend 
of a friend of your father's.

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:21.470
I'm bored here, too, so once I've eaten

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:23.540
my fill, I'll be leaving.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.670
I'm just a bird in a cage now.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:32.670
But one day I'll get out 
and fly much higher.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.440
That sounds lovely.

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:36.960
But you need to fill 
your stomach before

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:38.930
you can fly so high.

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:43.110
Most people would be creeped 
out by a middle school

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:45.940
student calling herself a bird.

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:47.880
Well, that's too bad.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:50.370
I would say I'm much more 
proficient at creeping out

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:51.830
grown-ups than you are.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:56.370
Take this Petri dish as 
a token of friendship.

00:16:57.650 --> 00:17:01.640
Have you heard of the slime mold, 
Physarum polycephalum?

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:04.320
It can find its way through mazes.

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:05.870
Really?

00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:20.240
It's a total breakdown!

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:20.180
A. latus

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:23.430
Diphtheroid

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:23.430
Another day gone by, and still 
no chance to make our move?

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:26.560
Who was the fool who 
said having friends over

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.790
would disrupt her daily routine?

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:31.960
Her skin is so perfect, there 
are no openings to invade from!

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:35.450
She's living the same well-regulated 
lifestyle as always!

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:37.010
This is a liability issue!

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:40.950
Vasinfectum

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:39.810
Let's court-martial the microbe 
who gave us that info!

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:40.950
Call the staff together!

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:40.950
Diphtheroid

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.840
Mutou!

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.260
Sleepy...

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:57.220
What? Have you been 
drinking all this time?

00:17:57.750 --> 00:18:00.360
Sorry, Haruka-san.

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:03.340
I finished all the wine in your cooler.

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:05.350
Hazuki-chan is sleeping on the sofa.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.210
All of it?

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:08.640
There were five bottles in there!

00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:11.360
The first one was really good.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.740
I can't remember anything 
after the second one.

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:17.020
You know, I've got another 
bedroom for you two.

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:18.860
Go there with Oikawa.

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:22.370
Haruka-san, you look 
cuter without makeup.

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:24.750
Sh-Shut up!

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:26.510
Hey, Haruka-san...

00:18:26.510 --> 00:18:27.370
What?

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:31.670
You're going to stay at the 
university for good, right?

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:35.630
Yes. If I leave, I'll be 
forced to get married.

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:38.160
You don't want to get married?

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:40.510
Because it was arranged for you?

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:42.510
You're drunk.

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:45.890
I don't want to walk a 
single step with a man

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:48.390
who won't even hold my hand on a date.

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:52.400
Now you know. Drink some 
water and go to sleep.

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.240
No way!

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:55.740
You're too cute!

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:56.900
It's true!

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:59.690
Haruka-san, you've changed.

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:03.310
Maybe it's because of Sawaki-kun, 
Misato-kun, and Kawahama-kun...

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:07.290
You seem happier when 
they're around, somehow.

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:09.280
Now, listen here...

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:27.530
I've changed? Don't say that.

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:30.890
I should carry Oikawa to her bed.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:33.000
Here's one that reeks of alcohol!

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:34.630
We got onto her with no problem!

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.400
She has no regard for her own health!

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:39.820
I've heard humans say 
that girls like this

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:42.410
are more attractive than flawless women.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.660
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:27.220
Moyashimon

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:27.220
Episode 9

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:27.220
Microbe Theater

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:27.220
Microbe Theater 9!

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:31.530
Now, what exactly is Surströmming?

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:34.230
It's sort of like Sweden's 
version of natto.

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:35.630
Oh, I see...

00:21:35.630 --> 00:21:37.230
That's too vague!

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:41.230
I will now explain how 
Surströmming is made.

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.360
Mediterranean Sea

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.610
Atlantic 
Ocean

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.820
Sweden

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.820
Baltic Sea

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.820
Europe

00:21:41.870 --> 00:21:44.740
Pregnant Pacific herring are 
caught in early spring,

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.740
Sweden

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.740
Baltic Sea

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:47.240
then packed into barrels 
in layers with salt

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:50.740
and allowed to ferment 
for a month or two.

00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:50.740
We're gonna brew!

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:54.250
The fermented herring 
are canned and sealed.

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:55.750
And it's done.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:56.780
That's it?!

00:21:56.780 --> 00:21:57.420
Indeed.

00:21:57.420 --> 00:21:58.960
Wait a minute!

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.750
Normally, canned foods

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:05.970
are only sealed after being heated 
to sterilize the contents.

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:07.510
But!

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:11.680
Surströmming cans are sealed 
without being sterilized.

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:13.760
We're gonna brew! We're gonna brew!

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:15.760
That's why fermentation continues

00:22:15.760 --> 00:22:17.770
within the can. Knock, knock.

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:19.770
Brew! Brew! Brew!

00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:29.640
In Microbe Theater 
Episode 10,

00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:29.640
We'll Do the Brewing.

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:31.700
You know, my first kiss was...

00:22:29.680 --> 00:22:34.700
Next Week: 
"The Gothic Lolita's Kiss"

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:34.880
Hey, Sawaki-kun, listen to me!
